1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,841
December 17th, 1903. A windy beach in North Carolina.

2
00:00:06,041 --> 00:00:08,857
A machine of spruce and cloth leaves the sand.

3
00:00:09,057 --> 00:00:11,963
Twelve seconds. One hundred and twenty feet.

4
00:00:12,163 --> 00:00:15,664
A man from the life-saving station took the photograph.

5
00:00:15,664 --> 00:00:18,014
He had never used a camera before.

6
00:00:18,964 --> 00:00:22,581
Four years earlier, two brothers ran a bicycle shop

7
00:00:22,581 --> 00:00:23,865
in Dayton, Ohio.

8
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,684
Wilbur and Orville Wright.

9
00:00:25,684 --> 00:00:27,995
Neither had a high school diploma.

10
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:32,396
In 1899, Wilbur wrote to the Smithsonian for everything

11
00:00:32,396 --> 00:00:33,587
it had on flight.

12
00:00:33,787 --> 00:00:34,949
I am an enthusiast,

13
00:00:34,949 --> 00:00:36,670
he wrote, but not a crank.

14
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,912
The man in charge there,

15
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:42,289
Samuel Langley, was building a flying machine of his

16
00:00:42,289 --> 00:00:42,775
own.

17
00:00:42,975 --> 00:00:46,067
The War Department gave him fifty thousand dollars.

18
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:48,634
On October 7th, 1903,

19
00:00:48,634 --> 00:00:51,296
it launched from a houseboat on the Potomac,

20
00:00:51,296 --> 00:00:53,765
and dropped straight into the river.

21
00:00:53,965 --> 00:00:56,554
Two days later, The New York Times said a

22
00:00:56,554 --> 00:00:59,871
real flying machine might take one to ten million

23
00:00:59,871 --> 00:01:00,526
years.

24
00:01:00,726 --> 00:01:03,343
On December 8th, Langley tried again.

25
00:01:03,343 --> 00:01:05,055
Same river. Same result.

26
00:01:05,805 --> 00:01:08,589
Nine days later, the Wright brothers were back on

27
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:09,466
that beach.

28
00:01:09,666 --> 00:01:12,251
Their whole effort had cost less than a thousand

29
00:01:12,251 --> 00:01:12,953
dollars.

30
00:01:13,153 --> 00:01:14,949
Orville flew first. By noon,

31
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:17,893
Wilbur stayed up for fifty-nine seconds.

32
00:01:18,093 --> 00:01:19,567
They wired their father:

33
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:22,323
Success. Four flights. Home for Christmas.

34
00:01:23,073 --> 00:01:25,649
The government spent fifty thousand dollars,

35
00:01:25,649 --> 00:01:27,255
and got a wreck in a river.

36
00:01:27,455 --> 00:01:30,584
Two bicycle mechanics spent less than a thousand,

37
00:01:30,584 --> 00:01:31,750
and got the sky.
